{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104637-no-metis-anymore","id":1104637,"title":"No Metis anymore","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-17T00:53:54-07:00","id":1104637,"title":"No Metis anymore","content":"So for some unspecified reason Garou doesn't produce metis anymore. Any Garou x Garou mating now results in a new werewolf. <br /> <br /> What would you think would happen and how would others react? Both mundane and supernatural sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T01:11:27-07:00","id":1104641,"title":"","content":"Do these not-Metis mature at a Homid rate or Metis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T01:21:11-07:00","id":1104644,"title":"","content":"Could be a hell of a story.<br /> Two warring factions could develop, one wants to change the Litany because then can muster forces with ease.<br /> The other side wants nothing to do with such blasphemy, the Litany is sacred and must not be changed.<br /> <br /> Another avenue could be the change in metis status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T01:29:23-07:00","id":1104645,"title":"","content":"Well... I'd imagine for most Garou in the Garou Nation, the biggest issue is actually the social upheaval as one of the Tenets of the Litany is now in serious question. But this would depend a bit on how this happens from the perspective of characters in-universe. If Gaia or Luna makes it clear that Garou on Garou mating is cool now, it's a very different issue than if it just suddenly happens and there's no reason to alter the Litany (meaning it would still be completely taboo culturally even if the child doesn't have the same issues as they would have before); esp. with the Perfect Metis legend.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, the biggest question becomes the very squicky issue of forced pregnancies. If Garou - Garou mating always produces at least one Garou child, and those children have no distinct drawbacks/issues besides taking a female Garou out of the fight, then the desperate End Times would lead to a massive upswing in pressure on female Garou to get knocked up (or be knocked up against their will) to rapidly grow the number of Garou (esp. if they grow at Metis rates, or Lupus rates for Lupus mothers). Maintaining kin bloodlines can be left to male Garou. This would be particularly unsettling with the BSD's already nasty ideas on making the next generation.<br /> <br /> Other supernaturals... aren't going to notice or care. At least not for a few years and even then they'd have to be paying enough attention to notice an upswing in werewolves running aorund.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T01:36:41-07:00","id":1104650,"title":"","content":"Depends heavily on if it is a sudden thing, or if it is from the start. And what the offspring looks like (homid,lupus, crinos baby without deformities?) affects it too.<br /> <br /> Because sudden things will basically make for an...interesting mental gymnasium to justify breeding for the apocalypse. Then again, I highly doubt it would be allowed, still. Mostly seen as a herald of the apocalypse among many others.<br /> <br /> And the BSDs just got their ultimate key to victory, unless only Gaian garou can produce non-sterile metis.<br /> <br /> If it was from the start, though. I actually think Garou Nation might be far FAR less uptight. Because eventually, new generations would change things, having grown up in the society rather than being introduced to it later. Plus, being able to continue the lineage means the werewolves would end up fracturing much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T02:05:50-07:00","id":1104653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104637-no-metis-anymore?p=1104641#post1104641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do these not-Metis mature at a Homid rate or Metis?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Metis rate.<br /> <br /> <br /> On unrelated note, I thought how it would serve to distance Garou from humanity, making them more anti-human as generations change and humans from somewhat simbiotic species turn into competitors and enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T02:09:22-07:00","id":1104655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104637-no-metis-anymore?p=1104653#post1104653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Metis rate.<br /> <br /> On unrelated note, I thought how it would serve to distance Garou from humanity, making them more anti-human as generations change and humans from somewhat simbiotic species turn into competitors and enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably, I think it might seriously improve the Garou as they become able to share their problems with spouses and equals so we no longer get up the screwed gender disparity as well as constant abuse of Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Metis are so common because Garou need someone they can share their burden with who understands, Litany be damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T02:27:14-07:00","id":1104656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104637-no-metis-anymore?p=1104653#post1104653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Metis rate.<br /> <br /> <br /> On unrelated note, I thought how it would serve to distance Garou from humanity, making them more anti-human as generations change and humans from somewhat simbiotic species turn into competitors and enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think it would go on the opposite direction. Look at how well in Forsaken 2nd edition the uratha have integrated themselves into humanity and general life. Garou Nation is a nervy as it is, because they basically never can truly exist in a calm society where their culture can evolve naturally. As CTPhipps above noted, the need for kinfolk as the only source of viable off-spring means the nation will forever switch generations and experiences randomly.<br /> <br /> In a natural societal process, things fracture, they move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T03:34:26-07:00","id":1104673,"title":"","content":"can't say I see it. Currently garou species, want they or not, are a satellite/symbiotic species with humans and wolves. If we remove the kinfolk and the need of them altogether, plus increasing reproduction 5-10 fold... what will hold them to be as humane as they are currently? or giving any value to humanity as it is now? It may take some time, but I think it will come to confrontation in the end, and not in a small scale. Repeat of impergium if you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T04:01:38-07:00","id":1104680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104637-no-metis-anymore?p=1104673#post1104673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can't say I see it. Currently garou species, want they or not, are a satellite/symbiotic species with humans and wolves. If we remove the kinfolk and the need of them altogether, plus increasing reproduction 5-10 fold... what will hold them to be as humane as they are currently? or giving any value to humanity as it is now? It may take some time, but I think it will come to confrontation in the end, and not in a small scale. Repeat of impergium if you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we aren't removing kinfolk, we aren't removing the homid form or the ability to breed with humans. Garou will still fall in love with humans, they will still keep to their families.<br /> <br /> Plus, the funny thing is that the more numbers you have, the more divisions you will find. Garou culture not being taught anew to new generations, but them growing up with it would mean there would be more incentive to change things. Or leave and form a new group. They might still call themselves Shadow Lord, but they would not match the tribe exactly anymore. And these new groups would breed and spread, maybe find likeminded humans, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T08:36:50-07:00","id":1104733,"title":"","content":"In my view, it would unbalance everything, as it would be much much easier to increase Garou population. Even cubs are very dangerous to many other creatures. Imagine living in a world where half are garou half are humans. Garou would rule the world. After some time, and possible after extinction of Vampires and other creatures they would start hunting humans or themselves. Studies have proven that wolfs live peacefully in their natural habitat because each pack lives far far from each other. But when you imprison packs in a space (when Earth no longer supports so many) they start the alpha male thinking. That's a nice Apocalypse scenario actually, as you stated before it will come to confrontation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13101-ntrlz","name":"Ntrlz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13101_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T09:31:04-07:00","id":1104747,"title":"","content":"I think a more interesting scenario would be if Garou were infertile with other Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T14:39:39-07:00","id":1104869,"title":"","content":"I think in at least one way, it might be a good thing for humans in that the possibility of a violent First Change in the middle of a crowded school/mall/subway train becomes much less... But for the most part I'm with Warpwind. If the werewolves no longer need humans at all and can rapidly expand their numbers at the same time, Humanity would very quickly be in some serious sh**.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T17:07:58-07:00","id":1104913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104637-no-metis-anymore?p=1104656#post1104656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually think it would go on the opposite direction. Look at how well in Forsaken 2nd edition the uratha have integrated themselves into humanity and general life. Garou Nation is a nervy as it is, because they basically never can truly exist in a calm society where their culture can evolve naturally. As CTPhipps above noted, the need for kinfolk as the only source of viable off-spring means the nation will forever switch generations and experiences randomly.<br /> <br /> In a natural societal process, things fracture, they move.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Forsaken have ALOT of differences from Garou though, most notably two Forsaken doesn't 100 percent make a new werewolf. They don't have Rage to separate them, they infact have a drive to form &quot;packs&quot; that readily include other outter tiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T17:11:22-07:00","id":1104915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104637-no-metis-anymore?p=1104869#post1104869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in at least one way, it might be a good thing for humans in that the possibility of a violent First Change in the middle of a crowded school/mall/subway train becomes much less... But for the most part I'm with Warpwind. If the werewolves no longer need humans at all and can rapidly expand their numbers at the same time, Humanity would very quickly be in some serious sh**.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Instead you'd have the vast majority of garou being people who've never been outside the Caern until their first change. Honestly I think Forsaken has it if you want to drop the sexual taboo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T18:01:18-07:00","id":1104937,"title":"","content":"I think that it is best if the majority of Garou are born to human or wolf parents. It gives them a perspective outside of the Garou Nation and always them to effectively interact with the society of their birth species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T03:18:41-07:00","id":1105017,"title":"","content":"How will the tribes react is maybe a better question. Should the red talon get their way humans will be decimated and no one could tell the red talon, that they &quot;need&quot; human kinfolk in the first place. It would lead to a huge increase in their population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T04:55:52-07:00","id":1105031,"title":"","content":"Which is a good point. I do not think that the Imperium would have ever ended if Garou-Garou mating reliably and safely produced fertile young. <br /> <br /> Now, an interesting twist would be to make a variation of the Kitsune Curse universal among Fera. When two Fera produce a Fera child, they each have a 50% chance of dying (meaning that each child born to two Garou would have a 25% chance of killing none of the parents, a 50% chance of killing one of the parents, and a 25% chance of killing both of the parents). That would justify the taboo and prevent Fera from becoming distant from their Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T05:10:03-07:00","id":1105033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104637-no-metis-anymore?p=1105031#post1105031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a good point. I do not think that the Imperium would have ever ended if Garou-Garou mating reliably and safely produced fertile young.<br /> <br /> Now, an interesting twist would be to make a variation of the Kitsune Curse universal among Fera. When two Fera produce a Fera child, they each have a 50% chance of dying (meaning that each child born to two Garou would have a 25% chance of killing none of the parents, a 50% chance of killing one of the parents, and a 25% chance of killing both of the parents). That would justify the taboo and prevent Fera from becoming distant from their Kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually say the earlier rule of 1 in 10 children of kitsune being fera alone would make things interesting enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T06:31:09-07:00","id":1105361,"title":"","content":"Based on my years of experience playing WTA, the Garou would lose without access to Metis Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T08:16:22-07:00","id":1105400,"title":"","content":"Metis Gifts could become General Gifts, like they exist in many other Fera species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T23:49:31-07:00","id":1109125,"title":"","content":"f garou can mate and have Garou babies that aren't metis, then they lose all need for wolf kinfolk entirely, and human kin become nothing more than catspaws in the mortal world. Humans are reduced to inconvenient chattel and wolves are an irrelevant precursor species. <br /> <br /> Why not have an impergium again, now that we have numbers and no need for humans? Why not just ignroe wolves entirely, they cost resources for no return. Kill the humans, let the dogs fend for themselves, we'll march to Malfeas and tear it apart fro mthe inside!<br /> <br /> And the Wyrm wins, pretty samn easy.<br /> <br /> The first tenet of the Litany isn't there to prevent metis. Metis are there to enforce that tenet. If you break the rule, well, you have pretty damned obvious evidence that you did it, huh? The point of the law is to keep garou tied to both sets of kinfolk, to PREVENT scenarios like what I described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T00:48:39-07:00","id":1109139,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back\">The Cat Came Back</a></b>, pretty much what I think too. Metis is there to tie Garou to both humans and wolves, otherwise competition between species kicks in. Wouldn't put it as a 'And the Wyrm wins, pretty samn easy'. wyrm doesn't win my simple merit of violence, or 'fighting' it would be impossible. But it would be fun times indeed. I don't see why Gaia wouldn't do it if the situation is desperate enough. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T03:51:42-07:00","id":1119452,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;no more Metis&quot; could happen two different ways. One is that the Metis breed is preserved, but they are now &quot;perfect Metis&quot; with no deformities or infertility to disgrace them; however, many of their gifts are associated with the suffering that comes from being Metis. Would the spirits refuse to teach those gifts to &quot;perfect&quot; meris breed Garou? The second way is to give the offspring the breed of the mother, and do away with the metis breed entirely. Then you lose what the breed contributes. Either way, Garou society would probably freak out and have trouble figuring out how to deal with the change, and what it would mean in the grand scheme of things. Would it be a sign of the apocalypse? Would it give hope that the war against the Wyrm could now be more winnable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T05:58:49-07:00","id":1119475,"title":"","content":"If it was from the begining, they would have genocided humans completely. They are more powerful than humans, and would have been so by a much larger margin during caveman times. They don't like humans. Humans would have gone the way of various hominids, and it would have happened much faster than that did. Vampires, at least Cainites, would have never existed. It's been implied that their have always been vampires of some sort, so something might exist to fill that cosmic niche, but it wouldn't be Cainites. It would be something as different from Cainites and Kue-Jin as they are from each other. Mages wouldn't exist, because the only sentient being in the world would be a race of static shamans/druids. No idea what would happen to all those avatars. Changlings likely would exist in some form, but not remotely the form we recognize. They would be creatures of the primal wyld. Werewolves can't become ghosts, right? So no ghosts as we understand it, as every spirit goes back to gaia, and become a wyld ancestor spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T18:27:46-07:00","id":1119720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104637-no-metis-anymore?p=1119475#post1119475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was from the begining, they would have genocided humans completely. They are more powerful than humans, and would have been so by a much larger margin during caveman times. They don't like humans. Humans would have gone the way of various hominids, and it would have happened much faster than that did. Vampires, at least Cainites, would have never existed. It's been implied that their have always been vampires of some sort, so something might exist to fill that cosmic niche, but it wouldn't be Cainites. It would be something as different from Cainites and Kue-Jin as they are from each other. Mages wouldn't exist, because the only sentient being in the world would be a race of static shamans/druids. No idea what would happen to all those avatars. Changlings likely would exist in some form, but not remotely the form we recognize. They would be creatures of the primal wyld. Werewolves can't become ghosts, right? So no ghosts as we understand it, as every spirit goes back to gaia, and become a wyld ancestor spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAn entire planet of Garou is something that might a good one off stop in 'sucked into a portal&quot; scenario in a larger campaign","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T18:51:20-07:00","id":1119729,"title":"","content":"Or you could have it that there are no Metis because Garou are not fertile with each other. The prohibition of Garou sleeping with Garou would then come from a concern about creating progeny rather than creating Metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:57:56-07:00","id":1119902,"title":"","content":"It's worth bearing in mind that in forsaken the uratha have stronger ties to humans because they're 100% &quot;homid&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}